@----------------------------------------
@node COMPILING
@prev INSTALLING
@next EXAMPLE
@toc INDEX
@{h1}Compiling code

Compilation is a two stage process.

@{h3}Compile the source code to assembly language
The following will compile a source file called demo.znc to a corresponding 
assembly file called demo.asm

.znc demo.znc

@{h3}Assemble the file to the executable binary
Using the NextBASIC Inline Assembler, you can then assemble the generated
assembly file to a binary.

.asm demo.asm

Now you should have file called demo in the DOT directory on your SD Card.
This DOT command can be tested by executing the following at the command line.

.demo
